<title>JAPAN: Vigilance needed on currency moves-Japan spokesman.</title>
<headline>Vigilance needed on currency moves-Japan spokesman.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary Seiroku Kajiyama said on Thursday currency movements must be carefully monitored as the Japanese economy is sensitive to rapid fluctuations in exchange rates.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have to keep close watch on currency movements as the Japanese economic structure is sensitive to rapid fluctuations in foreign exchange rates,&quot; Kajiyama told a news conference.</p>
<p>He was commenting on the recent renewed rise of the dollar against the yen.</p>
<p>&quot;Currency stability is important,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
